  "findings_resolved": [
    "Ordinary discovery uses an exact six-file exclusion and child-only barrier; direct/transitive frozen execution and audit-hook registration during collection have pure adverse coverage. Ordinary full collection has not been executed.",
    "Each frozen group runs in a fresh isolated child through its original guarded entrypoint, with original source hashes and case inventory checked. Real local runs confirm all220 cases on each exact supported runtime.",
    "Historical host/source requirements are explicit. Unsupported cases remain NOT_RUN and aggregate labels preserve this; no guessed socket hashes or rewritten frozen tests.",
    "Supervisor captures bounded output, enforces deadlines, kills/reaps on limits, preserves unknown shutdown/failures and sanitizes child environment. These adverse supervisor branches are mocked; actual integrations completed normally."
  ],
  "review_correction": "Lead initially read an earlier in-progress return missing host. Exact frozen9882cc86 already includes host/qualification; static assertion failed and no blocking finding report was written. Production defect claim withdrawn. V1.1 adds only useful supported-historical serialized coverage regression; production runner remains unchanged.",
  "limitations": [
    "This accepts the CI isolation component and focused frozen groups on local macOS runtimes, not Linux, full ordinary collection, all repository tests, original W03 correction, or remote green CI.",
    "Global hooks are isolated at the CI runner boundary; direct raw unittest discovery remains unsuitable for the six unchanged historical modules.",
    "The historical checks inspect the original bound host/socket source; they do not qualify a package installer, research runtime, PDF source, scientific result or complete project milestone.",
    "A supervisor with unreaped child reports failure/unknown shutdown; no such condition occurred in these actual runs. Authored failure tests remain scoped mock evidence.",
    "Earlier author failures and reconstructed historical source caveats remain unchanged in the two author handoffs."
  ],
